    "text": "I did not submit a candidate. The file's one real change can't be written into the contract from what I can see.\n\n- **What changed:** 6 of 24 rows have a `plan_code` outside the contract's allowed list (HMO, PPO, EPO, HDHP). The profile shows one distinct unknown value across those 6 rows, and the profile does not show what it is. Everything else matches the contract: column names, order, types, `member_id` pattern, `sex` codes and the optional `coverage_end`.\n- **Why I stopped:** Adding a plan code to `allowed` means knowing its exact spelling, and I don't. Guessing would be a loosening the file doesn't prove. Removing or widening the `allowed` list would be an unjustified loosening too. A deliberate new plan type is plausible, but a single unexplained value across 6 rows could also be a vendor error.\n- **Dry run of the unchanged contract:** 0 accepted, 6 rejected (`VALUE.NOT_ALLOWED:plan_code` \u00d76). The whole file is rejected with `FILE.BAD_ROW_RATIO`, since 25% exceeds the 5% limit.\n\nNext step: someone should confirm with the vendor what the new `plan_code` value is and whether it is intended. If it is a real new plan, I can add it to `allowed` in a version 2 contract and resubmit. If it is a vendor error, the file should be resent, which is the triage path.",
